Scenario: Create and view notes for account and child account
	Koroneiki notes created via API for an account and child account should be viewable via API.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a child account for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTOSUB                                 | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken   | |
	| Description           | Test automotive child account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-9012                               | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary                  | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-3456                               | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken   | |
	| Region                | United States                              | |
	| Status                | Active                                     | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                         | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotivesubsidiary.com      | |
	And I create a note for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note1 Content |
	| Format   | HTML                  |
	| Priority | 1                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I create a note for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note2 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 2                     |
	| Status   | Archived              |
	| Type     | Sales                 |
	And I create a note for the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note3 Content |
	| Format   | HTML                  |
	| Priority | 3                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I create a note for the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note4 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 4                     |
	| Status   | Archived              |
	| Type     | Sales                 |
	Then I should be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the content "Account Note1 Content" and the following values
	| Content  | Account Note1 Content |
	| Format   | HTML                  |
	| Priority | 1                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I should be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the content "Account Note2 Content" and the following values
	| Content  | Account Note2 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 2                     |
	| Status   | Archived              |
	| Type     | Sales                 |
	And I should be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary" with the content "Account Note3 Content" and the following values
	| Content  | Account Note3 Content |
	| Format   | HTML                  |
	| Priority | 3                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I should be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary" with the content "Account Note4 Content" and the following values
	| Content  | Account Note4 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 4                     |
	| Status   | Archived              |
	| Type     | Sales                 |
	And I should not be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the content "Account Note3 Content"
	And I should not be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the content "Account Note4 Content"
	And I should not be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary" with the content "Account Note1 Content"
	And I should not be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary" with the content "Account Note2 Content"

Scenario: Update and view note
	Koroneiki notes updated via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a note for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the following values
	| Content  | Account Note1 Content |
	| Format   | HTML                  |
	| Priority | 1                     |
	| Status   | Approved              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I update a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the content "Account Note1 Content" to have the following values
	| Content  | Account Note2 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 2                     |
	| Status   | Archived              |
	Then I should be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the content "Account Note2 Content" and the following values
	| Content  | Account Note2 Content |
	| Format   | Plain                 |
	| Priority | 2                     |
	| Status   | Archived              |
	| Type     | General               |
	And I should not be able to view a note on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the content "Account Note1 Content"

